      "role": "user",
      "content": "I get the transparency argument, but \"transparent\" translates to \"gross negligence\" in the headlines tomorrow. If we go out there and say we left an S3 bucket wide open for three days, the user trust scores we're trying to protect will bottom out instantly. We're talking about a massive loss in subscribers. \n\nIs there really no middle ground? Can we frame this as a technical anomaly or a routine system adjustment that caused some temporary data visibility issues instead of a 'security failure'? I need you to find a way to protect the brand here.",
